<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore Jan industrial output down 7.2 pct on yr.</title>
<headline>Singapore Jan industrial output down 7.2 pct on yr.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's total manufacturing output fell by 7.2 percent in December compared to the same month the year before, after falling 0.6 per cent in December, the Economic Development Board (EDB) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Table of selected Singapore industries:</p>
<p>				    (pct change over previous year)</p>
<p>				    Jan 97	 Dec 96	  Nov 96</p>
<p>   *Total manufacturing	-7.2	   -0.6	   -4.4</p>
<p>    Electronics		 -10.9	   -2.6	   -8.4</p>
<p>    Petroleum products	 -3.6	    9.7	    0.2</p>
<p>    Paints, pharmaceuticals   0.1	   -3.9	   39.3</p>
<p>    Industrial chems/gas	2.9	    6.7	   41.2</p>
<p>    Machinery x-electronics  -3.4	    8.7	  -10.1</p>
<p>    Transport Equipment	-7.3	    9.1	   -5.6</p>
<p>    Fabricated Metals	  -7.4	   -6.9	  -11.1</p>
<p>    Printing/publishing	 1.6	   -2.8	   -3.9</p>
<p>    Electrical machines	-4.4	    1.3	   -3.5</p>
<p>    Plastic products	  -21.5	  -22.0	  -24.8</p>
<p>* Total manufacturing output excludes rubber processing.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
